1
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:18,400
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:23,860
I kicked a pebble and it
went flying like a bear.

3
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:29,180
Clowning around,
right on the head of the PE teacher,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,700
they laughed at me for
staying so full of energy.

5
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:37,400
Even if I somehow stir up some energy,

6
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:38,640
Katsushika is where it's at.

7
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:40,980
One nightmare won't change a thing.

8
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:43,840
The streets are even kinder now.

9
00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:46,820
Because the crows are cawing,

10
00:00:46,820 --> 00:00:48,840
the sun is already setting.

11
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:51,900
Yakitori Honbari.

12
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:53,820
Will you look?

13
00:00:54,860 --> 00:00:57,460
Of the pointed hat...

14
00:01:30,420 --> 00:01:31,960
Ryotsu's late again

15
00:01:32,860 --> 00:01:34,900
Well, it's nothing new.

16
00:01:38,820 --> 00:01:42,180
Here he comes!

17
00:01:44,780 --> 00:01:46,200
You're late, Ryotsu!

18
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:48,920
My alarm clock didn't go off at all.

19
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:51,040
What's going on?

20
00:01:51,360 --> 00:01:52,840
Are you all in costume?

21
00:01:53,380 --> 00:01:54,520
What are you talking about?

22
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:57,980
Kei-chan told you to dress retro today,
didn't she?

23
00:01:58,460 --> 00:01:59,460
Did she?

24
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:03,460
We're leaving! Hurry up!

25
00:02:04,460 --> 00:02:05,760
Garigari!

26
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:07,300
Nick Star

27
00:02:27,060 --> 00:02:29,220
Nakagawa's company is amazing, isn't it.

28
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:32,520
Running a real Orient Express train,
no less!

29
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:35,040
And we can travel all
the way around Japan on it!

30
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:41,660
Yes, we wanted you to enjoy the atmosphere of
the real Orient Express while staying in Japan.

31
00:02:41,660 --> 00:02:47,340
The Nakagawa Group put all
its strength into this project.

32
00:02:47,880 --> 00:02:53,780
Being invited to the special train
before its opening is a real honor.

33
00:02:53,780 --> 00:02:56,740
Being colleagues with
Nakagawa really paid off

34
00:02:56,740 --> 00:03:00,180
Now, everyone,
please head to your private cabins.

35
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:05,240
As for the room assignments,
I'm in Room 1 and Reiko-san is in Room 2.

36
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:10,200
Room 3 is Chief Ohara, Room 4 is Ryo-san,
and Room 5 is Mr. Terai.

37
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:13,480
Who else has been invited besides us?

38
00:03:14,340 --> 00:03:18,700
Room 6 is Mrs. Christy Shiraishi,
a relative of mine.

39
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:22,740
Room 7 is for someone who is
also a rival of Nakagawa Railway,

40
00:03:23,160 --> 00:03:25,440
Mr. Ellery, president of Aokyu Railway.

41
00:03:26,220 --> 00:03:29,460
Room 8 is veteran actress Miyuki Takamura.

42
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:34,940
The infirmary is Kanawa
Zaiji Sōnyo Kuro Futsū Oshō.

43
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:41,420
And the person who came as a substitute for the
scheduled president of Yokomizo Paper Industry

44
00:03:41,420 --> 00:03:42,880
is staying in the infirmary.

45
00:03:44,900 --> 00:03:45,300
Yes.

46
00:03:46,720 --> 00:03:49,760
Excuse me, I'll check your tickets.

47
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:54,920
That's strange.

48
00:03:54,920 --> 00:03:56,720
What's wrong, Chief?

49
00:03:56,720 --> 00:03:58,280
Well, the thing is...

50
00:04:00,180 --> 00:04:02,340
I've lost it. Just as I feared.

51
00:04:02,340 --> 00:04:05,960
That's odd. I'm sure I had it.

52
00:04:05,960 --> 00:04:08,260
Get a grip, Chief.

53
00:04:08,920 --> 00:04:12,040
You're always so high and mighty with me,

54
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:15,800
but a chief should set an example.
What's going to happen if you act like this?

55
00:04:16,960 --> 00:04:19,980
Calm down, and let's think
it through from the beginning.

56
00:04:19,980 --> 00:04:20,400
What?

57
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:23,760
Knowing your personality,
when you left the house,

58
00:04:23,760 --> 00:04:26,940
you must have made sure the
invitation ticket was there, right?

59
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:28,160
Right.

60
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:34,000
And then at the station, when you boarded the train,
you folded it and tucked it into your commuter pass case, didn't you?

61
00:04:34,680 --> 00:04:35,440
That's right.

62
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:37,920
It's not here!

63
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:42,700
But I worried I'd drop it from my commuter pass case,
so I checked inside my hat.

64
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:44,760
That's right, inside the hat!

65
00:04:45,260 --> 00:04:46,780
Not there either!

66
00:04:46,780 --> 00:04:51,300
But then I worried the wind might blow my hat away,
so I checked my socks.

67
00:04:51,300 --> 00:04:51,600
Right!

68
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:55,340
Found it, found it!

69
00:04:55,820 --> 00:04:57,320
Good thing you found it, Chief.

70
00:04:58,160 --> 00:05:01,200
Wow, amazing, Ryo-chan!
You're like a great detective!

71
00:05:02,180 --> 00:05:04,100
That's nothing, easy as pie.

72
00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:08,180
Well, you lot are all just cheaters,
but I'm built differently up here.

73
00:05:14,180 --> 00:05:16,100
How do I look, Nakagawa? Suit me?

74
00:05:16,500 --> 00:05:19,620
Perfect, senior! A true great detective.

75
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:23,240
I think I'll head out
and do some investigating.

76
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:29,700
A suspicious light.

77
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:38,850
It's just head grooming.

78
00:05:38,900 --> 00:05:40,300
Quite dedicated

79
00:05:47,100 --> 00:05:50,620
Sorry about that. Are you hurt?

80
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:52,780
No, I'm fine.

81
00:05:52,780 --> 00:05:55,040
Something's on the ground.

82
00:06:04,860 --> 00:06:08,280
Damn it, can't I somehow crush this thing?

83
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:11,600
Excuse me.

84
00:06:29,160 --> 00:06:32,860
This is good!

85
00:06:33,420 --> 00:06:34,943
Ryo-chan,

86
00:06:34,993 --> 00:06:37,440
calm down and eat more properly.

87
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:40,960
a world-famous,
top-class chef has put his skills into this.

88
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:42,700
Please savor it carefully.

89
00:06:42,700 --> 00:06:45,360
I am savoring it, see? Like this.

90
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:47,160
Lero lero lero

91
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:50,480
A power outage, maybe?

92
00:06:51,140 --> 00:06:52,760
It's pitch black, I can't see a thing.

93
00:06:52,760 --> 00:06:53,680
Eek!

94
00:06:54,340 --> 00:06:55,300
What's wrong?

95
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:58,320
My bag...

96
00:06:59,900 --> 00:07:01,440
My meat is gone!

97
00:07:01,440 --> 00:07:02,480
Hey, hey.

98
00:07:05,860 --> 00:07:08,260
Ryo-san, you took my meat, didn't you?

99
00:07:08,260 --> 00:07:10,100
Whatever are you talking about?

100
00:07:11,060 --> 00:07:11,940
It's gone.

101
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:14,760
My diamond ring...

102
00:07:16,460 --> 00:07:17,960
You can't find it?

103
00:07:17,960 --> 00:07:18,540
Yes.

104
00:07:19,340 --> 00:07:22,400
I'm sure I put it in this bag, though.

105
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:23,420
Nowhere.

106
00:07:25,300 --> 00:07:27,800
Everyone, split up and search the train!

107
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:28,440
Yes, sir!

108
00:07:36,920 --> 00:07:37,800
Not here.

109
00:07:37,800 --> 00:07:38,760
Nothing here either.

110
00:07:38,760 --> 00:07:39,980
Same here.

111
00:07:39,980 --> 00:07:41,140
There's nothing.

112
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:45,440
If it's not here after searching this much,

113
00:07:47,600 --> 00:07:53,000
That was the first present my late husband ever gave me.
It's very precious to me.

114
00:07:53,620 --> 00:07:55,040
Without it, I...

115
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:55,740
I...

116
00:08:00,780 --> 00:08:02,200
During the blackout,

117
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:03,580
the diamond disappeared.

118
00:08:03,580 --> 00:08:05,660
But it wasn't dropped anywhere.

119
00:08:05,660 --> 00:08:07,240
That means...

120
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:08,140
it was stolen.

121
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:12,180
Everyone, don't move from here!

122
00:08:12,180 --> 00:08:14,360
The culprit is among us!

123
00:08:19,740 --> 00:08:20,860
Leave this case

124
00:08:20,860 --> 00:08:24,240
to the great detective Sherlock Ryotsu.

125
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:27,180
I'll find the culprit, I promise.

126
00:08:27,180 --> 00:08:28,600
Sherlock Ryotsu?

127
00:08:29,340 --> 00:08:30,700
That's right, Watson.

128
00:08:30,700 --> 00:08:31,940
Watson?

129
00:08:31,940 --> 00:08:33,160
Hold on a second.

130
00:08:33,160 --> 00:08:35,960
What are you going on about on your own?

131
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:39,660
I don't remember agreeing
to be bossed around by you.

132
00:08:39,660 --> 00:08:41,040
S-sorry.

133
00:08:41,500 --> 00:08:44,720
We haven't introduced ourselves yet.
We're with the police.

134
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:46,820
Please cooperate with the investigation.

135
00:08:46,820 --> 00:08:48,740
Well, in that case I understand.

136
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:50,160
Hey, everyone,

137
00:08:50,860 --> 00:08:51,260
yes.

138
00:08:51,720 --> 00:08:53,540
Thank you for your cooperation.

139
00:08:54,660 --> 00:08:57,900
Hey, Ryotsu! Enough with the detective act!

140
00:08:58,420 --> 00:09:01,360
Aren't you full of yourself, Chief?

141
00:09:01,360 --> 00:09:01,960
What?

142
00:09:01,960 --> 00:09:06,240
It was me who found the ticket the Chief lost,
with my brilliant deduction,

143
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:08,660
so who was it again?

144
00:09:08,660 --> 00:09:10,820
That's...

145
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:16,340
Leave this to the great detective,
Sherlock Ryotsu.

146
00:09:18,340 --> 00:09:20,720
Fine, I'll leave it to you for a while.

147
00:09:24,160 --> 00:09:27,500
The crime happened during that blackout,
in just ten seconds.

148
00:09:27,880 --> 00:09:31,780
The culprit took the diamond
from Countess Christie's bag.

149
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:35,060
In the rush,
the bag was dropped on the floor.

150
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:39,640
So the waitress who wasn't here
during the blackout is a mystery,

151
00:09:39,640 --> 00:09:43,140
and we can rule out the conductor,
Kyotaro Akagawa.

152
00:09:43,140 --> 00:09:46,120
Of course, the victim,
Countess Christie, too.

153
00:09:47,280 --> 00:09:49,920
And if we exclude us police officers,

154
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:53,160
the suspects are the four guests.

155
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:56,240
So I gave it some thought.

156
00:09:56,240 --> 00:10:00,700
And I've found someone among
them with a strong motive.

157
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:03,860
It was you.

158
00:10:03,860 --> 00:10:05,060
Mr. Ellery.

159
00:10:06,380 --> 00:10:07,380
That's absurd!

160
00:10:07,380 --> 00:10:09,040
Why would I?

161
00:10:09,580 --> 00:10:15,260
Nakagawa Railway and Seikyu Railway, which you
run as president, are rival companies, aren't they?

162
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:20,100
If the press finds out the
diamond went missing on this train,

163
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:23,220
Nakagawa Railway's reputation will plummet.

164
00:10:23,220 --> 00:10:25,100
No! Absolutely not!

165
00:10:26,880 --> 00:10:29,620
If you suspect me that much,
go ahead and search me.

166
00:10:30,240 --> 00:10:32,300
Very well, Watson.

167
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:33,920
Me?

168
00:10:33,920 --> 00:10:36,360
Go ahead and check, would you?

169
00:10:38,160 --> 00:10:39,220
Excuse me.

170
00:10:39,220 --> 00:10:40,180
Go ahead.

171
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:45,120
But Ryo-chan, even if we understand the motive,
that's not enough.

172
00:10:45,120 --> 00:10:47,260
We need ironclad evidence.

173
00:10:47,260 --> 00:10:47,920
Evidence?

174
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:50,480
I heard it with my own ears.

175
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:52,240
Earlier, Ellery...

176
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:56,560
Damn, is there no way
to nail this guy somehow?

177
00:10:56,560 --> 00:10:59,040
He definitely said that.

178
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:01,920
There's nothing anywhere, Ryo-san.

179
00:11:01,920 --> 00:11:03,960
What? That can't be.

180
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:05,540
Did you search him properly?

181
00:11:06,540 --> 00:11:09,800
That's odd. Didn't you say
earlier you'd definitely crush him?

182
00:11:09,800 --> 00:11:13,220
That was about this bean.

183
00:11:13,220 --> 00:11:14,000
Bean.

184
00:11:14,760 --> 00:11:16,460
You complete idiot.

185
00:11:17,040 --> 00:11:20,200
I told you to stop
playing detective already!

186
00:11:20,620 --> 00:11:24,680
Hunting for the culprit by pure
guesswork is why this happened.

187
00:11:24,680 --> 00:11:27,560
Wait, please hold on, Chief.

188
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:31,100
This time, I just got a little careless.

189
00:11:31,100 --> 00:11:34,180
Next time,
I'll definitely catch the culprit.

190
00:11:34,180 --> 00:11:36,440
Please give me one more chance.

191
00:11:38,220 --> 00:11:41,440
The crime happened in the
darkness during the blackout.

192
00:11:41,440 --> 00:11:44,380
So how could someone, in total darkness,

193
00:11:44,380 --> 00:11:47,060
have stolen the diamond?

194
00:11:47,060 --> 00:11:49,800
No, the culprit could see everything.

195
00:11:49,800 --> 00:11:52,640
Because the culprit is you.

196
00:11:52,640 --> 00:11:54,200
Black, no passing, King.

197
00:11:55,780 --> 00:11:57,640
Please, go ahead and search me.

198
00:11:58,560 --> 00:11:59,680
Watson-kun.

199
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:00,800
Yes.

200
00:12:01,940 --> 00:12:02,860
Excuse me.

201
00:12:04,600 --> 00:12:08,380
Ryo-chan,
how did you find the diamond in the dark?

202
00:12:08,780 --> 00:12:10,540
I saw it with my own eyes.

203
00:12:10,540 --> 00:12:14,960
Earlier, Kurofushi was
diligently polishing his own head.

204
00:12:14,960 --> 00:12:15,720
And?

205
00:12:16,060 --> 00:12:19,580
He used the light from that head in
place of the lights during the blackout.

206
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:23,440
Haa! This is so ridiculous,
there's no talking to you!

207
00:12:24,400 --> 00:12:25,780
It's not anywhere.

208
00:12:25,780 --> 00:12:26,560
Hmph!

209
00:12:26,720 --> 00:12:28,274
You utter fool!

210
00:12:28,324 --> 00:12:30,820
Once again,
you've made a huge mistake, haven't you?

211
00:12:30,820 --> 00:12:33,240
Wait, please.

212
00:12:33,240 --> 00:12:36,680
This time too,
I just wasn't quite thorough enough.

213
00:12:36,680 --> 00:12:39,140
Please, just give me one more chance.

214
00:12:40,460 --> 00:12:44,820
The guests on this train
are all wealthy people.

215
00:12:44,820 --> 00:12:48,640
Yet why was the diamond stolen?

216
00:12:49,140 --> 00:12:52,520
It's because the culprit is you.

217
00:12:52,520 --> 00:12:54,260
Ms. Miyuki Takamura.

218
00:12:55,940 --> 00:12:57,700
Please, go ahead and search me.

219
00:12:59,220 --> 00:13:00,180
Reiko-kun.

220
00:13:00,180 --> 00:13:01,680
Me?

221
00:13:02,280 --> 00:13:03,660
Search me, then.

222
00:13:04,780 --> 00:13:05,860
Excuse me.

223
00:13:06,820 --> 00:13:07,740
By the way, Ryotsu,

224
00:13:07,740 --> 00:13:09,880
why is the culprit Miyuki-san?

225
00:13:09,880 --> 00:13:11,920
I don't see the reason.

226
00:13:11,920 --> 00:13:15,240
No man is interested in diamonds.

227
00:13:15,740 --> 00:13:17,400
When it comes to diamonds, it's women.

228
00:13:18,180 --> 00:13:18,960
Evidence?

229
00:13:19,240 --> 00:13:20,700
There's nothing at all.

230
00:13:23,120 --> 00:13:24,580
No way, Ryo-chan.

231
00:13:24,580 --> 00:13:25,020
Tsk!

232
00:13:25,020 --> 00:13:26,860
You bungling idiot!

233
00:13:27,700 --> 00:13:28,940
This is your third time already!

234
00:13:28,940 --> 00:13:30,100
Weeee!

235
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:33,860
This time too,
it seems your scheming was a bit sloppy,

236
00:13:33,860 --> 00:13:35,900
but this time, for sure,

237
00:13:35,900 --> 00:13:37,320
Shut up!

238
00:13:37,320 --> 00:13:39,320
I won't be fooled again!

239
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:41,860
Chief, this time, absolutely,

240
00:13:41,860 --> 00:13:44,480
I will definitely find the culprit,
I promise!

241
00:13:45,580 --> 00:13:48,960
This crime was committed
with remarkable cunning.

242
00:13:48,960 --> 00:13:53,040
So the culprit is most likely
a seasoned professional.

243
00:13:53,680 --> 00:13:55,060
In other words, the culprit is...

244
00:13:55,840 --> 00:13:56,920
you!

245
00:14:00,780 --> 00:14:04,960
Just because he's the acting president of Yokomizo Paper,
we don't even know who he really is.

246
00:14:04,960 --> 00:14:06,420
He looks suspicious just by looking at him.

247
00:14:06,420 --> 00:14:09,500
He's the very picture of suspicion.

248
00:14:09,920 --> 00:14:11,980
Then why didn't you say so from the start?

249
00:14:12,740 --> 00:14:16,280
He's so suspicious that I
deliberately left him out, but...

250
00:14:16,280 --> 00:14:18,540
After all, you're the most suspicious one.

251
00:14:18,540 --> 00:14:22,580
Earlier, when people bumped into you, what
was that stuff you scattered in the aisle?

252
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:26,240
Isn't that exactly the
tool for stealing jewels?

253
00:14:28,140 --> 00:14:29,600
What's so funny?

254
00:14:29,600 --> 00:14:32,440
Those are my seven detective tools.

255
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:33,580
Detective.

256
00:14:35,820 --> 00:14:38,800
I am Edogawa Poirot, the detective.

257
00:14:40,920 --> 00:14:43,260
Edogawa Poirot.

258
00:14:47,500 --> 00:14:51,540
It seems the great detective Poirot's time has come,
after all.

259
00:14:51,540 --> 00:14:56,480
In fact, I suspected that something
serious might happen on this train,

260
00:14:57,700 --> 00:15:04,240
so I received a request from the president and quietly kept watch.
And, as I feared, the incident has occurred.

261
00:15:04,800 --> 00:15:10,060
But don't worry,
I shall solve this difficult case for you.

262
00:15:10,520 --> 00:15:19,940
Thank you for your hard work, amateur detective.
I watched for a while because it was entertaining, but it seems you're getting nowhere.

263
00:15:19,940 --> 00:15:20,260
Hey.

264
00:15:20,260 --> 00:15:23,660
Hey.

265
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:25,840
W-what is this?

266
00:15:27,020 --> 00:15:29,580
First, let's think about what
happened when the incident occurred.

267
00:15:29,580 --> 00:15:31,980
Let's recall it accurately.

268
00:15:32,760 --> 00:15:34,340
Reiko, do you have a mirror?

269
00:15:34,440 --> 00:15:35,720
I do, here you go.

270
00:15:36,300 --> 00:15:37,200
Thanks.

271
00:15:43,180 --> 00:15:44,400
What's the matter?

272
00:15:47,080 --> 00:15:48,220
It's nothing.

273
00:15:49,940 --> 00:15:55,660
Do it... a... so why, why,
how did things come to this? I see.

274
00:16:04,420 --> 00:16:10,700
It got stuck between my molar back then. Uh-oh,
at this rate I'll be framed as the thief.

275
00:16:10,700 --> 00:16:14,520
I have to do something about this.
Everyone had forgotten.

276
00:16:26,620 --> 00:16:34,680
The lights didn't come back on. So no one made any suspicious moves,
but the diamond is gone.

277
00:16:34,680 --> 00:16:42,060
Excuse me. How did they steal
the diamond from inside this bag?

278
00:16:43,100 --> 00:16:44,900
We were so close.

279
00:16:45,760 --> 00:16:51,720
How did the culprit find this bag
with the diamond in it in the dark?

280
00:16:52,180 --> 00:16:54,380
And how did they manage to
steal the diamond from inside it?

281
00:16:54,860 --> 00:16:56,900
Is this really that important?

282
00:16:56,900 --> 00:16:59,460
Damn it,
they went and left it in a place like that!

283
00:17:01,240 --> 00:17:03,520
A personal grudge against Christine.

284
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:06,020
It's you.

285
00:17:08,280 --> 00:17:09,160
Well, that's the thing.

286
00:17:10,680 --> 00:17:13,380
Don't mind me. Keep going, keep going.

287
00:17:29,200 --> 00:17:31,000
Problem number one.

288
00:17:32,220 --> 00:17:33,920
What's the motive?

289
00:17:34,340 --> 00:17:35,920
Problem number two.

290
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:42,660
Problem number three:
where do we hide the diamond?

291
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:13,860
...and so on, like what I just said.

292
00:18:15,120 --> 00:18:16,360
Think from the culprit's point of view.

293
00:18:16,360 --> 00:18:19,100
What possibilities can we consider?

294
00:18:19,100 --> 00:18:20,680
We should search for them.

295
00:18:20,680 --> 00:18:22,340
That's how we reach a conclusion.

296
00:18:25,280 --> 00:18:27,080
Therefore,

297
00:18:27,080 --> 00:18:30,740
The most distinctive feature of this case is

298
00:18:31,800 --> 00:18:33,680
Sorry to keep you waiting.

299
00:18:33,680 --> 00:18:34,860
So it's you.

300
00:18:34,860 --> 00:18:37,380
You're still dawdling
around with your deductions?

301
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:38,480
What?

302
00:18:40,200 --> 00:18:41,980
What do you know?

303
00:18:41,980 --> 00:18:44,400
It just hit me like a bolt of lightning.

304
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:48,540
This great detective,
Sherlock Ryotsu, has a brain that

305
00:18:48,540 --> 00:18:49,680
What?

306
00:18:49,680 --> 00:18:52,360
There's no motive, and there's no culprit.

307
00:18:52,360 --> 00:18:54,780
Then where did the diamond disappear to?

308
00:18:54,780 --> 00:18:57,160
No, it hasn't disappeared anywhere.

309
00:18:57,160 --> 00:19:00,800
In other words,
it never flew out of the bag.

310
00:19:02,020 --> 00:19:03,260
That's ridiculous.

311
00:19:03,260 --> 00:19:05,100
N-no way.

312
00:19:05,100 --> 00:19:07,280
It wasn't in the bag.

313
00:19:10,180 --> 00:19:11,840
Why don't you go and check it yourselves.

314
00:19:11,840 --> 00:19:12,620
Yes.

315
00:19:18,960 --> 00:19:20,140
Found it!

316
00:19:22,120 --> 00:19:23,780
That can't be.
I was sure it was there a moment ago.

317
00:19:23,780 --> 00:19:26,660
It must have gotten mixed in somewhere.

318
00:19:27,600 --> 00:19:28,960
Well, this is it, then.

319
00:19:31,500 --> 00:19:32,960
This is a fake.

320
00:19:33,380 --> 00:19:35,560
This one is...

321
00:19:36,080 --> 00:19:37,480
How can you tell?

322
00:19:37,480 --> 00:19:42,680
My ring has a loving message from
my husband engraved on the back.

323
00:19:42,680 --> 00:19:45,740
But this ring has no message engraved on it.

324
00:19:47,240 --> 00:19:48,560
What does that mean?

325
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:54,580
Well, Mr. Great Detective?
Is that all you've got?

326
00:19:55,840 --> 00:19:56,960
You bastard!

327
00:19:58,160 --> 00:20:02,820
Wait, now that I think about it,
we haven't searched your body yet, have we?

328
00:20:04,200 --> 00:20:06,200
I'm a detective, you know.

329
00:20:07,480 --> 00:20:15,080
Just because you say that doesn't mean you're not the thief.
Besides, what the hell were you doing in the corridor with those detective's seven tools?

330
00:20:15,660 --> 00:20:22,260
Hey, that's -
Check the Ueda Village electrical system! Got it, I'm going too.

331
00:20:23,260 --> 00:20:28,140
Nakagawa, Yokomizo, call the president!
I'm dialing now.

332
00:20:28,780 --> 00:20:31,160
Hello, this is Nakagawa, the police officer.

333
00:20:32,340 --> 00:20:33,140
Found it!

334
00:20:33,860 --> 00:20:35,360
Ryo-san, the timer!

335
00:20:35,780 --> 00:20:38,500
The flashlight was deliberately rigged.

336
00:20:39,480 --> 00:20:43,300
Yes, the president says he
doesn't know any Edogawa Poirot.

337
00:20:44,520 --> 00:20:46,620
So the mask has finally come off

338
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:49,900
Edogawa Poirot, you're the culprit!

339
00:20:53,920 --> 00:20:54,860
You're

340
00:20:54,860 --> 00:20:59,080
the Phantom Thief 1035

341
00:20:59,080 --> 00:21:01,000
Phantom Thief 1035?

342
00:21:01,460 --> 00:21:02,580
Don't you know?

343
00:21:02,660 --> 00:21:05,520
The jewel thief who's been causing
a stir in the world right now!

344
00:21:06,860 --> 00:21:09,260
I've certainly taken the ring.

345
00:21:10,080 --> 00:21:11,380
Give back the diamond!

346
00:21:11,520 --> 00:21:14,100
You damn detective, lying like that!

347
00:21:14,720 --> 00:21:19,660
I was going to stall until the next station,
but since I've been found out, it can't be helped.

348
00:21:21,360 --> 00:21:22,660
Farewell!

349
00:21:22,940 --> 00:21:23,660
Wait!

350
00:21:34,220 --> 00:21:37,120
You can't run anymore!
Now, hand over the diamond!

351
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:39,060
Hehehe, too bad!

352
00:21:39,340 --> 00:21:39,980
What?

353
00:21:40,220 --> 00:21:42,040
Then try and take it!

354
00:21:43,200 --> 00:21:43,460
Hmph!

355
00:21:43,900 --> 00:21:44,660
Haaah!

356
00:21:45,420 --> 00:21:46,160
Fwah!

357
00:21:46,320 --> 00:21:47,240
Go for it!

358
00:21:47,260 --> 00:21:48,480
Mmph!

359
00:21:50,160 --> 00:21:50,640
Mm?

360
00:21:51,880 --> 00:21:52,360
Ngh

361
00:21:52,360 --> 00:21:52,660
Ngh

362
00:21:53,180 --> 00:21:53,660
Ngh

363
00:21:53,660 --> 00:21:54,220
Ngh

364
00:21:54,220 --> 00:21:54,300
Ngh

365
00:21:54,300 --> 00:21:54,320
Ngh

366
00:21:54,320 --> 00:21:54,420
Ngh

367
00:21:54,420 --> 00:21:54,840
Ngh

368
00:21:54,840 --> 00:21:54,860
Ngh

369
00:21:54,860 --> 00:21:55,040
Ngh

370
00:21:55,040 --> 00:21:55,060
Ngh

371
00:22:04,740 --> 00:22:05,540
Got it!

372
00:22:18,940 --> 00:22:21,380
It's definitely my diamond.

373
00:22:21,980 --> 00:22:22,460
Thank you very much.

374
00:22:22,460 --> 00:22:23,060
Thank you very much.

375
00:22:23,540 --> 00:22:28,360
Please, with Sherlock Ryotsu on the case,
there's no mystery that can't be solved.

376
00:22:28,760 --> 00:22:29,820
Wow, you're amazing, Ryo-chan.

377
00:22:29,820 --> 00:22:32,580
Arresting a wanted criminal like that!

378
00:22:32,580 --> 00:22:34,560
Well, it's a great achievement, Ryotsu.

379
00:22:34,560 --> 00:22:36,700
No, no, it's nothing special.

380
00:22:36,700 --> 00:22:43,760
This guy stole an invitation from the home of Yokomizo Paper's president,
pretended to be a stand-in, and boarded this train.

381
00:22:43,760 --> 00:22:49,040
Then he used a timer to cause a blackout
and took Countess Christie's bag.

382
00:22:49,040 --> 00:22:51,860
But how could he see in the dark?

383
00:22:52,460 --> 00:22:55,460
His glasses had an infrared
scope built into them.

384
00:22:55,880 --> 00:22:58,040
And then he swapped the diamond for a fake.

385
00:22:58,540 --> 00:23:01,780
But Madam Shirasagi sensed
someone nearby and shook him off,

386
00:23:01,780 --> 00:23:05,580
the bag fell to the floor,
and the fake diamond bounced out of it

387
00:23:06,720 --> 00:23:08,700
and landed right on Terai's meat.

388
00:23:08,700 --> 00:23:11,060
Then I stole it and ate it,

389
00:23:11,060 --> 00:23:12,980
and it got stuck between my teeth.

390
00:23:12,980 --> 00:23:16,120
Thanks to that, I went through all that
trouble to get the diamond into the bag

391
00:23:16,120 --> 00:23:17,240
Ryo-san

392
00:23:18,840 --> 00:23:20,680
It got stuck between your teeth?

393
00:23:22,460 --> 00:23:23,460
So they borrowed a mirror

394
00:23:23,960 --> 00:23:26,140
And pretending a phone call came in,

395
00:23:26,140 --> 00:23:28,340
they tried to secretly put it back.

396
00:23:29,280 --> 00:23:31,660
The figure I saw outside the window,

397
00:23:32,040 --> 00:23:33,800
that was you, senpai, wasn't it?

398
00:23:34,180 --> 00:23:36,200
So it was you who ate my meat after all?

399
00:23:36,200 --> 00:23:37,400
It was you, Ryo-san.

400
00:23:38,060 --> 00:23:38,480
Hey.

401
00:23:38,480 --> 00:23:39,480
No, that's...

402
00:23:39,480 --> 00:23:40,420
Ryo-san.

403
00:23:42,040 --> 00:23:43,580
Everyone's sharp.

404
00:23:49,580 --> 00:23:50,920
Why are you on the step?

405
00:24:07,760 --> 00:24:10,660
There's a wall there.

406
00:24:11,520 --> 00:24:14,020
Well, there's surely a wall.

407
00:24:14,860 --> 00:24:19,360
Everyone, come visit our town!

408
00:24:20,240 --> 00:24:20,720
Thank you.

409
00:24:22,500 --> 00:24:23,900
Thank you for watching.

